    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.16) anchoring our offense. **Yelich** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Roki Sasaki; despite the pending lineup, his strong platoon split and projected cleanup spot maximize his scoring potential. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a top priority due to his elite sprint speed and a high-leverage leadoff role against Teng, where the dynamic platoon advantage compensates for the slight wind-in risk. **Yordan Alvarez** (72.42) rounds out our elite tier, as his elite xwOBA metrics allow him to transcend the moderate wind-in penalty at his home park, securing his spot as a daily must-start.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the bottom of the utility and middle infield spots, where **Chase Meidroth** (53.52) and **Luke Raley** (54.53) both grade out as marginal starts. **Meidroth** narrowly edged out potential alternatives due to the wind-out factor at his stadium, which slightly boosts his power potential against Houser. We are closely monitoring the status of **Gary Sanchez** and **Hyeseong Kim**; both are projected into the lineup, but their scores remain volatile due to their lower positions in the batting order. While **Junior Caminero** and **Colt Keith** would typically be in the conversation, they are both sidelined by confirmed rainouts, forcing us to rely on our active bench depth.\n\nLooking at the risk profile, the primary concern remains the stiff wind blowing in at several venues, which negatively impacted the ceilings of **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Yordan Alvarez**. However, **Trea Turner** retains a strong 69.64 score because the matchup against a slower-delivery pitcher maximizes his stolen base equity\u2014our highest priority in this scoring format. We will continue to track the official lineups for **Gary Sanchez**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Hyeseong Kim** to ensure no late-hour shifts require a pivot to bench options like **Josh Smith** or **Luis Pena**.",
